<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss sight deposits rise to 3,142.7 million Sfr.</title>
<headline>Swiss sight deposits rise to 3,142.7 million Sfr.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss National Bank said sight deposits rose by 80.5 million Swiss francs to 3.14 billion in the reporting period ended January 20.</p>
<p>Statement of January 20 in millions of Swiss francs:</p>
<p>					 Latest   Change since Jan 10</p>
<p> Sight deposits		   3,142.7	plus	80.5</p>
<p> Currency reserves	     47,428.6	minus     36.2</p>
<p> Domestic securities	    3,093.1	minus	2.1</p>
<p> Notes in circulation	  29,270.5	minus    955.3</p>
<p> Other call deposits		398.2	minus     62.5</p>
<p> Government time deposits     2,905.3	plus     680.0</p>
<p>An SNB spokesman said the latest change in sight deposits was routine. &quot;Everything is in the mainstream,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Borrowing at the emergency Lombard window fell by 0.5 million francs to 4.5 million in the reporting period.</p>
<p>Outstanding borrowing via the discount facility and swaps of money market certificates fell by 49.8 million francs to 399.8 million.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
